import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="One stock list. Every sale." description="Know what\u2019s on hand, what\u2019s reserved and what you can still sell.">
<PageHero eyebrow="The Kora product plan" title="One stock list. Every sale." lede="Know what\u2019s on hand, what\u2019s reserved and what you can still sell." />
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 prose-kora">
<h2>Every variant gets its own count</h2>
<p>Track products by SKU, including size, colour or pack. Begin with one stock location per merchant, with a data model that can support more locations later.</p>
<h2>Three numbers, fewer surprises</h2>
<p>On hand is the physical quantity. Reserved is the quantity held for orders. Available is on hand minus reserved. Payment confirms funds; pickup or dispatch records the goods leaving.</p>
<h2>A history behind every change</h2>
<p>Stock receiving, dispatch, accepted returns, damage and corrections each create a movement record. Corrections add a new entry with a reason instead of silently rewriting history.</p>
<h2>Designed for the last-item problem</h2>
<p>Every channel uses the same atomic reservation operation. Two concurrent checkouts cannot both reserve the last unit when the backend rules are enforced. An unpaid hold expires; paid holds remain until the order is resolved.</p>
<h2>What comes first</h2>
<p>Variants, opening counts, CSV import, receiving, adjustments, reservations, low-stock thresholds and basic purchase-cost tracking are in the proposed MVP. Batch expiry, serial numbers, bundles, supplier purchase orders and warehouse transfers need separate releases.</p>
<p><a href="/pilot" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the founding pilot</a></p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
